Here’s the whole sequence on the VDI. You only need to copy in one file, spn-migration.zip, and the script places everything else.

1. Put the zip in place. Save the attached spn-migration.zip to C:\repos\mix\ADO-GIT\, then run:

cd C:\repos\mix\ADO-GIT
Expand-Archive .\spn-migration.zip -DestinationPath $env:TEMP\kitnew -Force
robocopy $env:TEMP\kitnew\spn-migration .\spn-migration /E /XF spn-migration.config.psd1 /XD out

This updates the kit and keeps your config and out\ folder.

2. Open C:\repos\mix\ADO-GIT\spn-migration in VS Code.

3. Run the fix. Use the terminal, or Copilot Agent mode with only the terminal tool:

.\tools\Fix-SpnRepos.ps1

Type PUSH when it asks.

Where the files end up:

ADHPlatform/SPN, through a PR: CHANGELOG.md and .github/workflows/module-ci.yml and module-release.yml. spn-validation.yml and scripts/ are removed.
Deploy repo: .github/workflows/ServicePrincipal.yml (“5- Service Principal - Utility Pipeline”), oidc-test.yml, runner-test.yml, .github/actions/terraform-prepare/, Deployments/SPN/ and CoreInfra/SBX/NonProd/ (SPN.tfvars and modules_manifest.csv).

4. In the browser: merge the SPN PR. Then create the nonprod environment with AZURE_CLIENT_ID, AZURE_TENANT_ID and AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID, and run the workflow with custodian SBX, NonProd and the CencoraShared runner.

